# FoodSnap AI — environment variables
#
# The app runs in a graceful "demo / mock" mode when no provider is configured,
# so you can try the full flow without any credentials. Add ONE provider's key
# below to enable real AI image analysis.
#
# Provider selection:
#   - Leave AI_PROVIDER unset to auto-detect from whichever key is present
#     (Anthropic is preferred if both are set).
#   - Or set AI_PROVIDER explicitly to "anthropic", "gemini", or "mock".
# AI_PROVIDER=

# --- Option A: Anthropic (Claude) — https://console.anthropic.com/ ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the vision model (defaults to the cheapest tier, claude-haiku-4-5-20251001)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# --- Option B: Google Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/apikey ---
# GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY) enables the Gemini backend.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the vision model (defaults to the cheapest tier, gemini-2.5-flash-lite)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# --- Clerk (auth) — https://dashboard.clerk.com/ ---
# Source of truth for user identity. The analyzer itself stays public; only
# /profile and /results require sign-in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# Requires manual Dashboard configuration:
#   - Enable Google as a Social Connection (SSO)
#   - Enable "Username" as a profile field, if you want users to set one

# --- Supabase (saved analyses) — https://supabase.com/dashboard ---
# Persistence only, not auth. Service-role key, used server-side only —
# never exposed to the client, so no NEXT_PUBLIC_/anon key is needed.
# Run supabase/migrations/*.sql against your project before saving results.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
